 "text": "9/29/26, 9:39 AM\n\nWelcome Letter\n\nUse\n\nWhen you create or change a move-in, you can print a correspondence to be sent to the business partner, or generate a print order\nfor the correspondence. You have the following options:\n\ne Create welcome letter manually\nTo do this, choose the Welcome letter pushbutton in move-in processing.\n\ne Create welcome letter when data is saved\n\nTo have the system create a budget billing plan automatically when you save the move-in document, mark the WL checkbox\n(Create welcome letter automatically) in Customizing under |}Move-In/Out \u00bb Move-In > Define Move-In Control Parameters at\nDocument Level.\n\nIf necessary, you can also override the settings you have established in Customizing. To do this, choose |sExtras ' Control\nParameters \u201cJin move-in processing.\n\nWhen you create a welcome letter, specify an application form of the form class IS_U_CS_MOVE_IN_WELCOME_LETTER. In\naddition, you have to define the application form in Customizing under |} Utilities Industry Customer Service \u00bb Process\nExecution \u00bb Move-In/Out \u00bb Move-In \u00bb Define Welcome Letter \u00bb . You can find more information on creating an application\nform in the section on the \u201cPrint Workbench component.\n\nScreen Layout\n\nUse\n\nIn Customizing under |}Vove-In \u00bb Configure Tabs for Move-In Screen 3, you can configure various views for the data on the\nmove-in screen.These views are composed of tabs that you can use to organize the data into different logical units based on your\nrequirements.\n\nYou can maintain contract data in one of two ways:\n\ne Individual maintenance\nThe system displays the data of one contract only.\ne Overview maintenance\nThe system displays the data of up to five move-in documents allocated to the same contract.\n\nFor more information, see Customizing under |}}Move-In/Out Define System Parameters for Move-In and Move-Out\n\nYou can include standard and user-defined fields for the contract account and business partner in direct maintenance. To do this,\nuse the following enhancements:\n\ne EMBPOO3 (user subscreen in the business partner subscreen for move-in/out))\n\ne EMDCAOO]I (user subscreen for IS-U contract account)\n",
